1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:02:00,074
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:03,256 --> 00:02:06,066
-Celal Kün.
-You where born in 1987, in Maraş. (Commercial AD)

3
00:02:06,066 --> 00:02:08,136
Kahramanmaraş. (Kahraman=Hero, the word
was added after the war of independence)

4
00:02:08,136 --> 00:02:12,486
-His profession?
-Senior master sergeant. I was in the special forces.

5
00:02:12,486 --> 00:02:19,086
-Can you tell us about that day?
-It was the saddest day of my life. I didn't know.

6
00:02:19,848 --> 00:02:25,408
It could've been the happiest. I thought
that I was at the doors of heaven.

7
00:02:25,430 --> 00:02:27,680
I wanted to get in.

8
00:02:27,692 --> 00:02:30,342
But it was hell.

9
00:02:30,372 --> 00:02:34,882
Maraşlı will be on ATV in
11 January, Monday. (END of Commercial AD)

10
00:02:34,922 --> 00:02:39,372
No harm was done to any creature during
the filming of this series.

11
00:02:42,712 --> 00:02:48,402
May Allah bless your decision, daughter.
And may Allah keep you on this path.

12
00:02:50,032 --> 00:02:55,672
Firstly, you need to recite the kalima
shahadah. Repeat after me.

13
00:03:02,503 --> 00:03:06,503
I bear witness that...

14
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:16,140
I bear witness that...

15
00:03:16,140 --> 00:03:20,520
...there is no god but Allah...
-there is no god but Allah...

16
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:28,080
...and I bear witness that Muhammad
is the servant of Allah.

17
00:03:32,234 --> 00:03:35,974
Am I a Muslim now?

18
00:03:35,974 --> 00:03:45,544
You are in a word, daughter. But a Muslim
is the one who is trusted by everyone.

19
00:03:45,544 --> 00:03:50,924
The heart of a Muslim is the home of
trust, not treachery, daughter.

20
00:03:50,924 --> 00:03:55,114
Don't betray those who believe in you.

21
00:03:56,144 --> 00:04:00,144
You gave me shelter, you opened
your arms to me...

22
00:04:00,819 --> 00:04:06,249
...how can I betray you?
-Don't, daughter. Don't.

23
00:04:06,249 --> 00:04:12,849
Don't be a Muslim only by word.
Be a Muslim by your actions as well.

24
00:04:29,576 --> 00:04:32,586
Thank you, Selcan Hatun.

25
00:04:32,941 --> 00:04:39,031
-If you allow me...
-Of course, daughter. May Allah guide you.

26
00:04:55,908 --> 00:04:59,068
Targun Hatun!

27
00:05:03,127 --> 00:05:08,087
-What's wrong, Bala Hatun?
-I see that you learned to say Inshallah.

28
00:05:08,087 --> 00:05:11,307
I'm a Muslim now.

29
00:05:11,307 --> 00:05:14,357
Are you really?

30
00:05:14,371 --> 00:05:19,221
-Or are you playing some games?
-What games, Bala Hatun?

31
00:05:19,360 --> 00:05:25,740
-Don't you still trust me?
-Why did you hear or see to decide that?

32
00:05:26,998 --> 00:05:31,318
Osman Bey's words and actions
fascinated me.

33
00:05:32,137 --> 00:05:37,197
-I realized that his faith made him such--
-From now!

34
00:05:37,952 --> 00:05:41,952
You'll never speak of Osman Bey's name!

35
00:05:46,084 --> 00:05:49,994
Know that I'm watching you.

36
00:05:55,133 --> 00:05:59,133
I won't take him out of my words
nor of my heart...

37
00:05:59,350 --> 00:06:03,350
...but you will step away, Bala.

38
00:06:08,768 --> 00:06:12,768
Have you finished the job
I've given you?

39
00:06:12,871 --> 00:06:19,971
-Flatyos ran away, sir.
-You'll get your reward in Christ's heaven.

40
00:06:22,707 --> 00:06:28,947
I'm not serving the pope
for Christ's heaven...

41
00:06:28,947 --> 00:06:32,947
...but to send the Turks to hell, sir.

42
00:06:36,179 --> 00:06:39,329
Sir, they are coming.

43
00:07:12,518 --> 00:07:15,968
It's time.

44
00:08:13,181 --> 00:08:17,911
Brother, we should be on our way.
We must find Flatyos.

45
00:08:18,227 --> 00:08:22,567
If we can't find that dog,
we can't answer Osman Bey!

46
00:08:22,567 --> 00:08:26,567
What is it that you can't answer, Göktuğ?

47
00:08:29,397 --> 00:08:33,397
Flatyos ran away, Dündar Bey.

48
00:08:33,985 --> 00:08:38,995
It has only been a
few days but...

49
00:08:39,049 --> 00:08:43,319
...now you lost a man?

50
00:08:45,544 --> 00:08:51,324
It seems that your bey made a mistake
by giving you this mission.

51
00:08:57,022 --> 00:09:05,702
-Someone helped him, Dündar Bey.
-Even if so, it's your responsibility.

52
00:09:07,402 --> 00:09:10,792
It's your fault.

53
00:09:13,868 --> 00:09:17,008
What is it?

54
00:09:18,741 --> 00:09:25,621
He ran away with this. Someone gave
this to him at night!

55
00:09:33,434 --> 00:09:40,004
Come on, alps. We'll find that dog.
Come on!

56
00:10:27,920 --> 00:10:31,920
From Oghuz Khagan to his sons...

57
00:10:32,132 --> 00:10:35,822
...three bows and three arrows
were left.

58
00:10:35,822 --> 00:10:41,882
His sons conquered the world
with those bows and arrows.

59
00:10:42,846 --> 00:10:46,846
They founded great states.

60
00:10:46,846 --> 00:10:50,556
With those states,
they brought justice to the realm...

61
00:10:50,556 --> 00:10:55,526
...and spreaded the laws.

62
00:11:00,421 --> 00:11:08,921
Now, whoever has the blessing of Allah,
who has the light of the laws...

63
00:11:09,174 --> 00:11:13,814
...he is the great Turkish khagan...

64
00:11:13,814 --> 00:11:17,814
...and others are his subjects.

65
00:11:37,335 --> 00:11:43,415
When the Seljuk sultan bowed down
to the Mongols at Kösedağ...

66
00:11:43,415 --> 00:11:49,135
...the great Turkish khaganete
tore down, the order went to lose.

67
00:11:49,549 --> 00:11:57,439
The unity was broken. Turkish
tribes spread all over the world.

68
00:11:58,432 --> 00:12:03,762
Osman Bey, it's the time of
bringing the order back...

69
00:12:03,762 --> 00:12:08,622
...and uniting the tribes.

70
00:12:37,853 --> 00:12:43,413
'Welcome, Bala Hatun'
'Welcome, Bala Hatun'

71
00:12:55,707 --> 00:12:59,497
Thank you, women.

72
00:13:05,467 --> 00:13:08,977
Sit, please.

73
00:13:35,585 --> 00:13:41,005
From now, you are the head hatun
of the tribe.

74
00:13:42,134 --> 00:13:46,134
Come on, we are all listening to you.

75
00:13:46,194 --> 00:13:53,194
Women. Every new bey comes with
his own methods and manners.

76
00:13:54,289 --> 00:13:59,949
As the wife of Osman Bey, so have I.

77
00:13:59,949 --> 00:14:06,979
As the time comes, I'll tell you how I
work and what I expect from you.

78
00:14:08,634 --> 00:14:14,344
But, firstly, I want you to know
and don't forget...

79
00:14:14,489 --> 00:14:20,439
...that Osman Bey doesn't only need
ghazis but also scholars now.

80
00:14:23,623 --> 00:14:29,143
I'll bring teachers to teach how
to read.

81
00:14:29,143 --> 00:14:33,413
'May Allah bless you'
'May Allah bless you'

82
00:14:33,413 --> 00:14:35,693
Thank you.

83
00:14:37,814 --> 00:14:46,074
I want you to make sure that your
children benefit from those teachers.

84
00:14:57,535 --> 00:15:00,295
Thank you.

85
00:15:09,938 --> 00:15:14,658
I have to do this.
I have to.

86
00:15:23,408 --> 00:15:29,338
Osman Bey, you are looking
at those documents now.

87
00:15:29,428 --> 00:15:36,638
How to kick the Mongols
out of these lands...

88
00:15:36,689 --> 00:15:43,809
...how the order will be rebuilt when
the Anatolia becomes Turkish again...

89
00:15:43,908 --> 00:15:49,968
...and how the unity will be assured,
are written in it.

90
00:15:55,297 --> 00:16:02,387
Osman Bey, now the duty is yours and
your children's.

91
00:16:16,340 --> 00:16:20,630
Bamsı Bey, now...

92
00:16:23,243 --> 00:16:27,243
...we have the escrows.

93
00:16:28,143 --> 00:16:32,143
I'll protect them at the
risk of my life.

94
00:16:33,495 --> 00:16:39,345
I'll struggle for my state to be
a world power...

95
00:16:39,528 --> 00:16:44,328
...for the Turkish khaganate...

96
00:16:44,769 --> 00:16:48,329
...to be formed again.

97
00:16:48,486 --> 00:16:53,416
Until...
Until...

98
00:16:54,072 --> 00:17:01,622
...the sun of the laws can shine again,
unity can be formed again...

99
00:17:03,577 --> 00:17:09,607
The three bows and three arrows
will come together again.

100
00:17:15,740 --> 00:17:21,220
Long live Osman Bey!
Long live Osman Bey!

101
00:17:22,341 --> 00:17:31,791
This is what your grandfather Süleyman
Shah and your father Ertuğrul expects!

102
00:17:46,910 --> 00:17:54,930
Come on, come on, Osman Bey!
Now return and start to build order.

103
00:17:56,347 --> 00:17:59,867
Thank you, Bamsı Bey.

104
00:18:36,444 --> 00:18:43,144
Oh my Allah, you destined
such a leader to the Turks...

105
00:18:43,144 --> 00:18:45,514
...thank you.

106
00:18:47,138 --> 00:18:50,878
Thank you...

107
00:18:58,310 --> 00:19:01,920
Come on, women.

108
00:19:01,920 --> 00:19:05,920
Let us drink our sherbet
and do our prayers.

109
00:19:07,964 --> 00:19:11,254
Enjoy it.

110
00:20:25,921 --> 00:20:31,911
-Osman is going. Should we follow him?
-We'll follow Osman a lot.

111
00:20:33,384 --> 00:20:37,964
We must find the hole he is
hiding, and get the plans.

112
00:20:51,267 --> 00:20:55,997
There will be a single man
in front of you...

113
00:20:55,997 --> 00:21:00,821
...if you underestimate him,
none of you will survive.

114
00:21:01,301 --> 00:21:05,396
Be cautious.
We'll kill Bamsı, get the plans...

115
00:21:05,396 --> 00:21:09,266
...and leave here at once.

116
00:21:33,860 --> 00:21:39,920
My dear friend Flatyos!
It's so nice to see you here.

117
00:21:43,636 --> 00:21:47,636
So, your visit to the Kayı tribe
is over.

118
00:21:48,667 --> 00:21:52,667
Good. Come, tell me.

119
00:21:54,398 --> 00:21:58,398
What did you see,
what did you hear...

120
00:22:04,551 --> 00:22:09,911
-Did you save me, Nikola?
-I would do it but I got help.

121
00:22:14,776 --> 00:22:18,776
-From whom?
-Old Roman bishop.

122
00:22:18,776 --> 00:22:24,686
Holy, mighty, respectable pope, we
can name him. An unexpected ally.

123
00:22:25,836 --> 00:22:31,436
-I think it's something like the god's hand.
-The Pope in the Kayı Tribe...

124
00:22:31,885 --> 00:22:37,705
I must admit that they are very good
at their work, Flatyos.

125
00:22:37,705 --> 00:22:41,705
They have a man in everywhere.

126
00:22:43,240 --> 00:22:47,240
Now the war starts again, my dear friend.

127
00:22:47,402 --> 00:22:53,602
Osman became the bey, Nikola.
He united the tribes. They are more now.

128
00:22:53,759 --> 00:22:58,079
He controls all the alps,
he is with Yavlak Arslan.

129
00:22:58,079 --> 00:23:03,369
I know, Flatyos.
I know. Stop talking about Osman.

130
00:23:03,369 --> 00:23:09,029
Look, we took a man from his tribe
on the first day of his reign.

131
00:23:10,570 --> 00:23:16,160
-They were about to take my head.
-But have they?

132
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:21,370
They couldn't. So, don't be sad anymore.

133
00:23:22,081 --> 00:23:28,091
We are stronger than before now, Flatyos.
We'll hurt more now.

134
00:23:28,669 --> 00:23:32,669
And since Osman has the whole
responsibility of the tribe now...

135
00:23:32,718 --> 00:23:37,988
...when we hurt someone,
we'll be hurting Osman.

136
00:23:37,988 --> 00:23:41,988
Just like that, Flatyos.
Just like that.

137
00:23:41,988 --> 00:23:48,678
We'll hurt more than before. And you
know me, I like to hurt.

138
00:23:54,515 --> 00:24:00,035
Flatyos, maybe you should change
your shoes.

139
00:24:33,804 --> 00:24:39,424
My Bey, we sent the alps everywhere.
But we couldn't find Flatyos.

140
00:24:39,424 --> 00:24:42,924
That dog should've paid for
his crimes!

141
00:24:45,964 --> 00:24:49,964
From the first day, how can you
make such a mistake?

142
00:24:51,935 --> 00:24:55,935
What will we do?

143
00:24:55,935 --> 00:24:59,935
Will we doubt you when we go out
to take care of something?

144
00:25:00,673 --> 00:25:06,713
What are you saying, my bey? Don't you
know? We rather die than disobey you.

145
00:25:06,713 --> 00:25:11,443
What is this, then?
You couldn't keep a single man!

146
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:19,940
Not only a man. Our archenemy who
killed our alps, Osman Bey.

147
00:25:21,272 --> 00:25:27,862
My nephew brought the man in chains
and you lost him. Tell me, Osman Bey!

148
00:25:37,651 --> 00:25:40,881
Get out.

149
00:26:14,386 --> 00:26:16,896
Osman Bey!

150
00:26:27,993 --> 00:26:31,243
Bala?
Bala...

151
00:26:33,319 --> 00:26:35,719
Osman...

152
00:26:41,479 --> 00:26:43,819
Bala!

153
00:26:45,975 --> 00:26:51,095
Bala! Bala!
Bala, are you all right?

154
00:26:54,105 --> 00:26:58,605
Open your eyes.
Bala, open your eyes!

155
00:27:02,877 --> 00:27:08,867
Open your eyes. What's wrong?

156
00:27:09,125 --> 00:27:13,125
Bala, Bala!

157
00:27:36,431 --> 00:27:39,021
Bala!

158
00:27:50,822 --> 00:27:55,712
-Osman!
-Aunt! Come, aunt!

159
00:27:57,099 --> 00:28:03,119
Bala, daughter! Breath!
Leave us, go!

160
00:28:05,753 --> 00:28:11,753
Aunt, aunt!
What did she eat?

161
00:28:13,743 --> 00:28:18,943
Osman, she hardly breaths!
What will we do?

162
00:28:19,440 --> 00:28:22,220
-Bala!
-Poison...

163
00:28:24,468 --> 00:28:27,148
Open your eyes, Bala...

164
00:28:30,098 --> 00:28:33,828
-Bala!
-Osman Bey!

165
00:28:33,828 --> 00:28:38,428
I heard about Bala Hatun and I ran here.
I know about these things. I might help.

166
00:28:38,428 --> 00:28:42,998
Come on, be quick. Come on!
Come on!

167
00:29:02,208 --> 00:29:05,508
Her uvula is swelled out.

168
00:29:06,600 --> 00:29:11,500
-I know the cure. I'll prepare the mix.
-Be quick.

169
00:29:16,592 --> 00:29:20,942
Osman, Osman!

170
00:29:20,942 --> 00:29:25,866
Are you sure to trust that girl now?

171
00:30:06,607 --> 00:30:08,657
Here!

172
00:30:13,185 --> 00:30:16,535
It must be close.

173
00:31:09,718 --> 00:31:11,921
We are starting.

174
00:31:26,585 --> 00:31:29,545
Be aware.

175
00:31:47,149 --> 00:31:51,709
The hands that reach to the escrows,
get chopped, chopped, chopped!

176
00:31:55,030 --> 00:31:59,940
Escrows are my honor!

177
00:32:08,563 --> 00:32:14,613
These eyes saw the secret place!
These eyes saw the secret place!

178
00:32:14,613 --> 00:32:18,475
They haven't!
They haven't!

179
00:32:18,475 --> 00:32:23,525
There are no eyes!
There are no eyes!

180
00:32:43,600 --> 00:32:48,600
You came to your death!
You came to your death!

181
00:32:49,545 --> 00:32:53,545
No, we came to your funeral, Bamsı Bey!

182
00:33:17,506 --> 00:33:20,636
Bala, open your mouth.

183
00:33:29,458 --> 00:33:34,398
Help us, my Allah.

184
00:33:44,387 --> 00:33:47,807
Selcan Hatun, help me.

185
00:34:12,003 --> 00:34:16,003
You are the mightiest, my Allah!

186
00:34:18,964 --> 00:34:22,434
Now, we will wait.

187
00:34:35,267 --> 00:34:38,877
My love...

188
00:34:41,101 --> 00:34:45,101
My love...

189
00:34:46,083 --> 00:34:49,433
Help her, my Allah...

190
00:36:17,624 --> 00:36:24,544
You can't reach to the escrows
that Bamsı protects! You can't

191
00:37:08,026 --> 00:37:10,496
O' Bamsı the Big.

192
00:37:27,541 --> 00:37:33,401
O' Bamsı the Big.
It's your turn now.

193
00:37:34,491 --> 00:37:40,151
Look, Ertuğrul Bey is gone too.

194
00:37:42,036 --> 00:37:46,036
And Bamsı...

195
00:37:46,067 --> 00:37:50,637
...Hafsa awaits you.

196
00:37:52,348 --> 00:37:55,748
Your children await.

197
00:38:06,442 --> 00:38:10,442
Your prophet awaits.

198
00:38:13,892 --> 00:38:17,172
You should give your life now.

199
00:38:20,093 --> 00:38:25,023
My Allah, thank you.

200
00:38:27,413 --> 00:38:31,413
For making me a martyr.

201
00:38:33,232 --> 00:38:37,225
My Allah, make
me a neighbor...

202
00:38:37,225 --> 00:38:41,685
...to our prophet.

203
00:38:48,680 --> 00:38:51,490
Amin.

204
00:38:55,763 --> 00:38:59,313
It's my turn now.

205
00:38:59,742 --> 00:39:03,422
I protected the escrows, my bey.

206
00:39:14,592 --> 00:39:17,992
I protected the escrows.

207
00:39:46,743 --> 00:39:51,363
-Bala, Bala!
-Osman...

208
00:39:51,643 --> 00:39:54,853
Thank Allah, thank Allah!

209
00:39:59,996 --> 00:40:05,996
Thank Allah...
Thank Allah...

210
00:40:09,055 --> 00:40:13,055
Thank Allah...

211
00:40:17,640 --> 00:40:21,150
Thank Allah she came round.

212
00:40:39,017 --> 00:40:43,487
Aygül, Gonca...

213
00:40:47,974 --> 00:40:51,974
...put Targun Hatun to
cage tent.

214
00:41:07,390 --> 00:41:11,610
Osman Bey, what--

215
00:41:16,321 --> 00:41:20,321
You are making a mistake!
Osman Bey!

216
00:41:24,336 --> 00:41:29,236
It's over, daughter.
It's over.

217
00:42:15,405 --> 00:42:19,405
We'll kill him and get the escrows.

218
00:42:37,263 --> 00:42:41,263
Come, come...

219
00:42:41,480 --> 00:42:45,480
...come to the hell you are
looking for.

220
00:42:53,491 --> 00:42:57,771
Look who is here!
We are here, Bamsı Bey!

221
00:43:11,926 --> 00:43:15,926
Osman didn't leave his man alone!

222
00:43:16,991 --> 00:43:23,461
Valiants, victory belongs
to those who have faith!

223
00:43:23,998 --> 00:43:26,648
Ya Allah!

224
00:44:31,557 --> 00:44:35,397
I always liked you, Bamsı Bey.

225
00:44:36,320 --> 00:44:41,830
Now, I'm starting to like you, Cerkutay!

226
00:44:55,277 --> 00:44:57,827
Bamsı Bey!

227
00:45:18,244 --> 00:45:20,574
Abdurrahman Ghazi!

228
00:45:20,574 --> 00:45:23,294
God damn you, Osman!

229
00:45:27,908 --> 00:45:33,038
So, Abdurrahman Ghazi,
just like the old days, huh?

230
00:45:33,929 --> 00:45:35,639
Yes, brother.

231
00:45:40,917 --> 00:45:46,457
With a single arm, we are
enough for all of them, Bamsı.

232
00:45:49,669 --> 00:45:53,669
Thank Allah, thank Allah, brother.

233
00:45:54,998 --> 00:46:03,368
Lads, there is a cover there.
You'll find two chests. Bring them here.

234
00:46:03,368 --> 00:46:04,868
All right, my bey.

235
00:46:15,252 --> 00:46:20,762
My bey, what were you doing
here alone?

236
00:46:25,896 --> 00:46:31,956
Cerkutay, alps don't ask questions.

237
00:46:54,923 --> 00:46:58,923
What are in the chests, my bey?

238
00:47:04,516 --> 00:47:07,266
Cerkutay.

239
00:47:08,187 --> 00:47:12,437
So, Abdurrahman Ghaz, tell me.
Where did you come from?

240
00:47:12,437 --> 00:47:18,917
-Osman Bey sent us, brother. Osman Bey.
-Oh, Osman Bey...

241
00:47:18,917 --> 00:47:24,097
...mashallah to him.

242
00:47:36,007 --> 00:47:40,007
He wanted me to come.

243
00:47:46,333 --> 00:47:52,903
Cerkutay, I'm glad you came.
Without you, how would've we be like?

244
00:47:54,366 --> 00:47:58,336
I'm glad you did, Cerkutay.

245
00:47:59,231 --> 00:48:06,331
Alps, we need to take these chests
to Osman Bey at once.

246
00:48:08,322 --> 00:48:14,002
Cerkutay, come with us.
Come with us, Cerkutay.

247
00:48:15,733 --> 00:48:17,753
Come on, come one.

248
00:48:25,172 --> 00:48:30,082
-What will we do now?
-We'll follow them.

249
00:48:39,176 --> 00:48:41,346
Bala.

250
00:48:51,620 --> 00:48:56,220
-Are you better now?
-I'm fine, Osman.

251
00:48:56,381 --> 00:49:00,101
I'm better now.

252
00:49:09,156 --> 00:49:13,156
Why are your eyes wet?

253
00:49:13,156 --> 00:49:18,266
-You are the bey now.
-You are the bey's wife now.

254
00:49:19,029 --> 00:49:23,029
Your wife lays here, Osman Bey.

255
00:49:24,907 --> 00:49:28,907
Where is your heir?

256
00:49:32,809 --> 00:49:36,809
I pray for a child.

257
00:49:37,994 --> 00:49:43,234
I wish it to be my child,
not another woman's.

258
00:49:43,425 --> 00:49:47,885
So do I, Bala.
So do I.

259
00:49:47,885 --> 00:49:51,885
I want you to give me a heir.

260
00:49:51,885 --> 00:49:55,885
I want my children to carry
your noble soul.

261
00:49:56,239 --> 00:50:01,909
I want to see the jihad love of Kayı beys,
and your pure heart on them.

262
00:50:02,701 --> 00:50:06,701
You want your blood to continue
through me.

263
00:50:08,572 --> 00:50:14,802
But, if Allah hasn't destine it...

264
00:50:16,546 --> 00:50:20,546
...it will go through someone else, Osman.

265
00:50:26,501 --> 00:50:33,121
I pray, Bala.
I ask it from Allah.

266
00:50:34,782 --> 00:50:38,102
I await.

267
00:50:41,869 --> 00:50:47,849
-What else can we do?
-You await, Osman Bey.

268
00:50:48,822 --> 00:50:52,822
But the enemy doesn't.

269
00:50:56,070 --> 00:51:00,070
Look what they've done to me.

270
00:51:01,397 --> 00:51:07,487
I'll make them pay for this.
I'll make them pay.

271
00:51:08,289 --> 00:51:12,289
Don't worry, Bala.

272
00:51:14,207 --> 00:51:18,207
You need an heir, Osman.

273
00:51:22,528 --> 00:51:26,078
Until that heir borns...

274
00:51:27,794 --> 00:51:33,124
...neither you nor me will
be free of these troubles.

275
00:51:35,191 --> 00:51:40,461
Neither you nor our tribe
will have a future.

276
00:51:46,917 --> 00:51:53,357
Would Targun try this if you had
an heir?

277
00:52:00,498 --> 00:52:02,518
Bala...

278
00:52:02,783 --> 00:52:04,143
...Bala...

279
00:52:06,275 --> 00:52:10,275
Don't think about these.

280
00:52:10,768 --> 00:52:14,378
Think about our love.

281
00:52:15,483 --> 00:52:19,483
Think about our love and smile.

282
00:52:20,335 --> 00:52:22,005
Come on.

283
00:52:23,430 --> 00:52:29,650
Come on, smile.
Bring the sun to my tent with your smile.

284
00:52:33,179 --> 00:52:36,879
Just like that.

285
00:52:38,800 --> 00:52:42,460
My heart is already warm.

286
00:52:46,117 --> 00:52:51,447
Recover as soon as you can.
All the Kayı women await you.

287
00:52:52,061 --> 00:52:55,871
They are worried about you.

288
00:54:09,283 --> 00:54:11,753
May I enter, my bey.

289
00:54:14,773 --> 00:54:17,043
Come.

290
00:54:28,218 --> 00:54:33,518
-Come, Master Davud.
-We have news from Saltuk, my bey.

291
00:54:35,769 --> 00:54:38,119
Dündar Bey...

292
00:54:42,030 --> 00:54:45,350
What did Dündar Bey do?

293
00:54:45,391 --> 00:54:50,391
He left the tents to meet
with Nikola.

294
00:55:11,376 --> 00:55:18,626
-What did he do?
-Saltık sent word before leaving.

295
00:55:21,521 --> 00:55:27,521
He'll meet with Nikola's men
and they will go to the meeting point.

296
00:55:38,905 --> 00:55:42,905
Dündar Bey, Süleyman Shah's son.

297
00:55:51,785 --> 00:55:55,785
Went to the heathen, is that so?

298
00:55:56,917 --> 00:56:00,917
He still dreams of being a bey.

299
00:56:04,464 --> 00:56:07,294
Uncle...

300
00:56:08,734 --> 00:56:10,774
Uncle...

301
00:56:11,829 --> 00:56:15,419
What else do you want?

302
00:56:15,990 --> 00:56:19,650
What are you after?

303
00:56:23,847 --> 00:56:31,157
What are you forcing me into?

304
00:56:41,589 --> 00:56:47,109
My bey, what will we do
if Osman Bey hears this?

305
00:56:47,109 --> 00:56:52,139
He will not hear it, Saltuk.
He will not hear it.

306
00:57:38,045 --> 00:57:47,045
Dündar Bey, we live in strange times.
It's getting harder to find someone smart.

307
00:57:49,334 --> 00:57:54,104
Do you see yourself as a smart man?

308
00:57:54,162 --> 00:58:01,532
No, no, I'm a man who can act weird
and do unexpected things.

309
00:58:05,516 --> 00:58:10,986
Like Osman, I'm a bit crazy.

310
00:58:13,360 --> 00:58:18,980
When there are no smart people between
two crazy people...

311
00:58:18,980 --> 00:58:24,650
...the innocent people pay for it.

312
00:58:25,157 --> 00:58:31,287
-What do you want from me, Nikola?
-What I want is known, Dündar Bey.

313
00:58:31,287 --> 00:58:38,077
I want Kulucahisar. And you want to
be a bey, don't you?

314
00:58:38,600 --> 00:58:44,250
We'll take the title from Osman
and give it to you.

315
00:58:51,238 --> 00:58:57,708
Don't make your decision right away,
Dündar Bey. Think about it.

316
00:58:59,236 --> 00:59:05,136
You ask me to betray my own tribe.

317
00:59:08,180 --> 00:59:12,180
Dündar Bey.

318
00:59:12,180 --> 00:59:16,730
If I were you, I would never
call it treason.

319
00:59:18,763 --> 00:59:24,733
Think about it, you are the bey,
you sit on the fur.

320
00:59:24,733 --> 00:59:28,718
And as soon as you sit...

321
00:59:28,718 --> 00:59:34,158
...both Rome and the Mongols
attacks.

322
00:59:36,910 --> 00:59:44,520
-And you want me to give you Kulucahisar?
-As a sign of our friendship.

323
00:59:49,680 --> 00:59:55,440
We are in times that we need to remember
that peace is a virtue, Dündar Bey.

324
00:59:55,440 --> 01:00:00,620
Rome made agreements with everyone.

325
01:00:00,620 --> 01:00:04,080
Why wouldn't it make agreements
with the Turks?

326
01:00:05,136 --> 01:00:09,136
But because of the kinds of Osman...

327
01:00:20,390 --> 01:00:22,780
Open the door.

328
01:00:41,259 --> 01:00:44,899
I never trusted you.

329
01:00:45,686 --> 01:00:49,686
I didn't do anything.
On the contrary...

330
01:00:49,686 --> 01:00:52,766
...I saved Bala.

331
01:00:53,531 --> 01:00:58,151
You first poisoned her,
then saved her.

332
01:00:58,518 --> 01:01:01,028
Is that so?

333
01:01:04,998 --> 01:01:08,998
How do I know that you didn't?

334
01:01:14,170 --> 01:01:17,613
Is it a lie that your mother tried
to poison all the Kayı beys?

335
01:01:17,613 --> 01:01:21,503
Don't talk about my mother!

336
01:01:32,945 --> 01:01:36,945
You want Bala to die...

337
01:01:37,681 --> 01:01:42,911
...because you also love Osman.
Confess it.

338
01:01:46,064 --> 01:01:51,714
Will you kill someone tied?
Kill me! Come on!

339
01:01:51,714 --> 01:01:55,714
If I wasn't going to answer Osman Bey...

340
01:01:55,714 --> 01:01:59,364
...I would cut your tongue here.

341
01:02:03,791 --> 01:02:07,791
I pity you, Aygül.

342
01:02:07,791 --> 01:02:12,251
I pity you for leaving your love
to someone else.

343
01:02:13,192 --> 01:02:16,892
Shut up! Shut up!
Shut up!

344
01:02:16,892 --> 01:02:22,332
Now, you will answer to Osman Bey!

345
01:02:22,332 --> 01:02:28,282
Move now! Move, I said!
Move! Move!

346
01:02:39,985 --> 01:02:44,635
-Can I enter, my bey?
-Come, Aygül.

347
01:02:57,643 --> 01:03:03,513
Even if I forgive you,
the laws won't.

348
01:03:18,186 --> 01:03:21,546
Targun Hatun.

349
01:03:23,555 --> 01:03:29,385
Don't waste my time and
accept your crime.

350
01:03:31,623 --> 01:03:35,243
I'm not guilty.

351
01:03:36,214 --> 01:03:39,884
Why should I accept it.

352
01:03:44,999 --> 01:03:48,999
You said that you'll be a Muslim.

353
01:03:49,789 --> 01:03:53,439
Does a Muslim lie?

354
01:03:56,854 --> 01:04:00,674
Did you believe it?

355
01:04:04,842 --> 01:04:08,732
I wanted to believe.

356
01:04:10,275 --> 01:04:14,025
I loved you, Osman Bey.

357
01:04:15,806 --> 01:04:19,556
I wanted you to like me.

358
01:04:20,280 --> 01:04:23,800
I wanted you to marry me.

359
01:04:23,866 --> 01:04:29,486
Did you convert even though
you didn't believe?

360
01:04:38,073 --> 01:04:42,073
Aren't you afraid of committing a sin?

361
01:04:48,414 --> 01:04:52,414
I'm not afraid to burn in hell for you.

362
01:04:57,772 --> 01:05:01,772
You'll die in hell for me, huh?

363
01:05:04,387 --> 01:05:10,877
But I live in heaven.
I live with angel.

364
01:05:19,214 --> 01:05:23,924
Who sealed my heart,
who tied my hands...

365
01:05:25,618 --> 01:05:30,308
Who imprisoned me in her eyes...

366
01:05:36,783 --> 01:05:40,783
I wish I spared some of that poison...

367
01:05:42,150 --> 01:05:46,150
...and didn't run here with the
cure like an idiot.

368
01:05:50,146 --> 01:05:55,226
If you weren't a woman,
I would kill you here.

369
01:05:57,311 --> 01:06:01,311
Because of the things you had
done to me and my wife...

370
01:06:01,435 --> 01:06:07,135
...and for your false conversion,
I banish you!

371
01:06:08,176 --> 01:06:13,386
You and your father will never
come to these tents.

372
01:06:20,643 --> 01:06:24,173
And you, Göktuğ.

373
01:06:24,173 --> 01:06:28,173
You failed me.
You couldn't guard my enemy.

374
01:06:31,982 --> 01:06:36,392
I don't want to see you either.
You won't come to these tents.

375
01:06:36,392 --> 01:06:41,472
You are spurring all the things my brother
and I did, for a single mistake.

376
01:06:42,406 --> 01:06:46,406
That's what one would expect from a
bey who banish the woman...

377
01:06:46,795 --> 01:06:50,795
...who says that she would burn.
in hell for him.

378
01:06:58,014 --> 01:07:02,014
You have never been worthy
of your brother.

379
01:07:04,926 --> 01:07:08,456
Get out of my face!

380
01:07:16,498 --> 01:07:20,498
You will not come to these tents again!

381
01:07:21,789 --> 01:07:24,139
Go!

382
01:08:25,401 --> 01:08:29,401
So, she won't come to these tents
again. Is that so, Osman Bey?

383
01:08:31,873 --> 01:08:37,063
-It's true.
-Is that the punishment of killing your wife?

384
01:08:37,063 --> 01:08:43,123
Releasing her? Would you be so
merciful to someone else?

385
01:09:01,481 --> 01:09:04,991
Are you jealous of her, Bala?

386
01:09:07,614 --> 01:09:11,337
Can't I have some other
reason for that?

387
01:09:11,337 --> 01:09:14,917
Tell me too, then.

388
01:09:21,926 --> 01:09:27,636
Including you, everyone will
know things...

389
01:09:28,570 --> 01:09:30,830
...but...

390
01:09:32,727 --> 01:09:37,517
...only I will know everything.

391
01:09:43,927 --> 01:09:47,177
Is that so, Osman Bey?

392
01:09:49,086 --> 01:09:51,616
Yes.

393
01:10:13,956 --> 01:10:16,376
Yes.

394
01:11:13,361 --> 01:11:18,521
-What's wrong, Boran Alp?
-Nothing, Dündar Bey.

395
01:11:28,263 --> 01:11:33,703
Dündar Bey, Osman Bey wants you
in his tent.

396
01:11:54,649 --> 01:11:59,929
What's wrong, Dündar Bey?
Had something happen?

397
01:12:01,276 --> 01:12:08,136
Either my death order or my
salvation.

398
01:12:10,098 --> 01:12:16,218
What are you saying, Dündar Bey?
What death?

399
01:12:19,377 --> 01:12:22,897
Who can kill you?

400
01:12:33,749 --> 01:12:41,359
If you think things are going bad,
send word to Yavlak Arslan to save me.

401
01:12:49,522 --> 01:12:53,522
What did you do, Dündar Bey?

402
01:12:53,804 --> 01:13:00,934
Stay calm, woman. I'll figure something
out. Stay calm.

403
01:13:02,958 --> 01:13:06,198
Come on. Go.

404
01:13:16,485 --> 01:13:19,945
What did you do to us, Dündar Bey?

405
01:15:20,032 --> 01:15:23,302
Uncle.

406
01:15:26,220 --> 01:15:29,780
Brother of my uncle.

407
01:15:35,174 --> 01:15:41,734
-Do you know why I called you?
-I know, Osman Bey. I know.

408
01:15:47,364 --> 01:15:50,180
So, you know.

409
01:15:50,530 --> 01:15:53,630
You wonder where I was.

410
01:15:56,779 --> 01:16:02,519
Boran, take my uncle's weapons.

411
01:16:29,464 --> 01:16:32,744
Come, uncle.

412
01:16:34,931 --> 01:16:37,371
Come.

413
01:16:56,208 --> 01:16:59,408
Where were you?

414
01:17:02,988 --> 01:17:08,998
-Where were you, uncle?
-I went to Nikola, nephew.

415
01:17:19,897 --> 01:17:23,897
Why did you do that?

416
01:17:24,034 --> 01:17:30,074
He wants your head. He offers
co-operation.

417
01:17:41,734 --> 01:17:45,294
Is that so?

418
01:17:45,473 --> 01:17:48,883
Is that so?

419
01:17:50,972 --> 01:17:53,242
Yes.

420
01:17:54,152 --> 01:17:59,212
And, what did you say?
What did you say?

421
01:18:01,839 --> 01:18:08,089
For him to not get suspicious,
I got mad and shouted first.

422
01:18:10,195 --> 01:18:14,775
''Do you think I'm a traitor?'' I said.

423
01:18:16,067 --> 01:18:21,927
But then I acted like I was convinced.

424
01:18:21,927 --> 01:18:26,847
He spoke and I listened.

425
01:18:31,848 --> 01:18:35,759
I didn't say anything certain but...

426
01:18:35,759 --> 01:18:40,649
...but he thinks that I'm trapped.

427
01:18:45,369 --> 01:18:48,469
Uncle...

428
01:19:04,765 --> 01:19:07,835
Is that so?

429
01:19:13,027 --> 01:19:16,827
So, you say that.

430
01:19:18,184 --> 01:19:22,184
-Yes.
-But...

431
01:19:26,900 --> 01:19:30,900
It looks like you are trapped, uncle.

432
01:20:06,118 --> 01:20:09,798
Why did you do that?

433
01:20:22,131 --> 01:20:27,991
For you to trap him when you want.

434
01:20:30,344 --> 01:20:35,384
If I had invited him, he would
get suspicious.

435
01:20:35,384 --> 01:20:39,384
But he invited me.

436
01:20:39,944 --> 01:20:46,634
Now, he wants to use
me against you.

437
01:20:50,287 --> 01:20:56,277
But, you should use me against him,
nephew.

438
01:21:22,813 --> 01:21:26,813
Those who come from
the bey's family...

439
01:21:30,991 --> 01:21:34,991
...shouldn't get bleed...

440
01:21:42,489 --> 01:21:44,849
...here...

441
01:21:47,433 --> 01:21:51,053
...for this reason...

442
01:21:52,275 --> 01:21:54,855
...if...

443
01:21:56,984 --> 01:22:00,984
...they betray...

444
01:22:06,041 --> 01:22:10,351
...then, they...

445
01:22:13,159 --> 01:22:17,159
...get strangled...

446
01:22:18,228 --> 01:22:22,108
...with bow string.

447
01:22:29,396 --> 01:22:32,676
Uncle!

448
01:22:38,456 --> 01:22:42,336
Without asking me...

449
01:22:43,548 --> 01:22:47,318
...how can you act on your own?

450
01:22:48,521 --> 01:22:52,181
How can you step over the bey?

451
01:22:57,052 --> 01:23:01,772
Wasn't it you who said that
there is a traitor in the tents?

452
01:23:05,654 --> 01:23:10,824
If I had come and told you,
they would tell it to Nikola.

453
01:23:16,848 --> 01:23:22,548
But, I wanted to be seen like
I was acting on my own.

454
01:23:30,204 --> 01:23:37,164
Don't worry, uncle. There won't be
any traitor left in the tents.

455
01:23:39,328 --> 01:23:44,318
I will kill them all. All of them.

456
01:23:44,318 --> 01:23:49,598
Everyone who schemes from my back
will end badly.

457
01:23:50,402 --> 01:23:56,852
Those who don't want the same fate,
will act accordingly.

458
01:24:15,734 --> 01:24:21,144
My bey, Bamsı Bey is here.
He is wounded.

459
01:24:36,753 --> 01:24:39,803
And from now...

460
01:24:42,452 --> 01:24:48,082
...even if it's for me,
nothing will be done...

461
01:24:48,178 --> 01:24:51,818
...without my information.

462
01:24:54,342 --> 01:24:58,182
It shall be known.

463
01:25:30,804 --> 01:25:35,524
The heathens, the heathens
attacked me, Osman Bey.

464
01:25:35,778 --> 01:25:41,798
But, there is nothing
to concern.

465
01:25:48,821 --> 01:25:52,821
You say so, huh?

466
01:25:53,353 --> 01:25:58,493
But I don't think so, Bamsı Bey.
Not really.

467
01:26:00,280 --> 01:26:03,420
Be careful.

468
01:26:15,995 --> 01:26:19,995
Long you live, Osman Bey!

469
01:26:20,491 --> 01:26:24,491
Don't worry about the escrows.

470
01:26:24,491 --> 01:26:28,861
Abdurrahman Ghazi will hide them
in somewhere safe.

471
01:26:29,211 --> 01:26:34,681
We don't have time to lose.
We must invite the beys to meeting.

472
01:26:34,681 --> 01:26:40,191
Send word to frontiersmen. I'll talk to
them about something important in Söğüt.

473
01:26:41,254 --> 01:26:46,594
-As you order, my bey.
-Thank you, lad.

474
01:26:54,980 --> 01:26:57,180
Bamsı Bey.

475
01:27:01,059 --> 01:27:04,639
So, they followed us, huh?

476
01:27:07,276 --> 01:27:11,276
If they haven't known where
we were going...

477
01:27:11,917 --> 01:27:15,917
...they wouldn't follow us...

478
01:27:16,055 --> 01:27:21,135
...but where did they learn it?
I can't understand.

479
01:27:22,202 --> 01:27:27,802
They don't know where we went,
but why we went.

480
01:27:30,636 --> 01:27:36,696
That's why they followed, Bamsı Bey.
That's how they learned.

481
01:27:37,047 --> 01:27:43,147
How did they hear of the secret that only
Ertuğrul Bey and I knew?

482
01:27:44,671 --> 01:27:49,711
Bamsı Bey, they are...

483
01:27:50,828 --> 01:27:54,828
...are like our old enemies...

484
01:27:58,879 --> 01:28:02,879
...my father's enemies.

485
01:28:06,334 --> 01:28:10,334
They are stronger enemies than
heathen Nikola.

486
01:28:13,913 --> 01:28:17,913
Stronger, you say, huh?

487
01:28:18,783 --> 01:28:24,483
So it seems.
So it seems.

488
01:28:33,490 --> 01:28:36,950
So it seems.

489
01:28:37,485 --> 01:28:41,025
The escrows are in danger, Bamsı Bey.

490
01:28:41,025 --> 01:28:47,845
Everyone is in danger, Bamsı Bey.
We must hurry. The circle narrows.

491
01:28:49,331 --> 01:28:53,331
My father would want me to work
with my brothers.

492
01:28:53,331 --> 01:28:55,741
That's what I'll do.

493
01:28:56,752 --> 01:28:59,042
I'll do...

494
01:29:00,592 --> 01:29:04,592
...and we'll stand strong.
-You are right, Osman Bey.

495
01:29:04,592 --> 01:29:08,592
That's what your father would
want.

496
01:29:11,638 --> 01:29:14,218
Osman Bey.

497
01:29:16,493 --> 01:29:20,123
There is something else that
is important.

498
01:29:33,235 --> 01:29:37,025
What is it, Osman Bey?

499
01:29:59,226 --> 01:30:03,226
Osman Bey went to Bamsı's tent.

500
01:30:03,276 --> 01:30:07,276
He'll tell Osman about the incident.

501
01:30:07,332 --> 01:30:11,332
What we were looking for was
in those chests.

502
01:30:13,502 --> 01:30:17,502
Welcome, welcome, welcome.

503
01:30:17,502 --> 01:30:20,982
If it wasn't for you, I wouldn't
be able to sell all these.

504
01:30:21,951 --> 01:30:25,951
Abdurrahman Ghazi is missing.

505
01:30:31,425 --> 01:30:39,375
No, mister, no! Instead of selling it
to you at that price, I rather smash it!

506
01:30:39,375 --> 01:30:43,185
Have some mercy!
Have some mercy!

507
01:30:43,781 --> 01:30:50,801
All right, all right. Have it your way.
He is a good trader.

508
01:31:02,715 --> 01:31:08,265
This man named Abdurrahman.
Keep your eyes on him all the time.

509
01:31:08,527 --> 01:31:12,727
We'll go and talk to this Osman.

510
01:31:36,033 --> 01:31:38,133
Open it, lad.

511
01:31:59,769 --> 01:32:01,349
Bamsı Bey.

512
01:32:04,760 --> 01:32:09,010
-It's my father's will.
-It is.

513
01:32:23,257 --> 01:32:29,237
-He says that he choose me to be the bey.
-Of course, Osman Bey.

514
01:32:38,932 --> 01:32:42,132
Tells me to give duties
to my brother and uncle.

515
01:32:43,785 --> 01:32:46,735
To keep their hearts warm.

516
01:32:46,754 --> 01:32:50,374
He is right, Osman Bey.
He is right.

517
01:32:57,418 --> 01:32:59,258
Bamsı Bey.

518
01:33:01,602 --> 01:33:04,932
Why didn't you tell me before.

519
01:33:06,003 --> 01:33:12,543
He told Abdurrahman Ghazi to keep it
until the end of the elections.

520
01:33:14,455 --> 01:33:16,015
Osman Bey.

521
01:33:18,108 --> 01:33:21,098
Have you read it until the end?

522
01:33:42,323 --> 01:33:44,823
My father tells me to find a new wife.

523
01:33:50,287 --> 01:33:51,827
He orders me.

524
01:33:52,234 --> 01:33:56,304
He is right, Osman Bey.
He is right, son.

525
01:33:56,393 --> 01:34:01,673
Now, as long as you don't
have an heir...

526
01:34:01,737 --> 01:34:04,897
...your reign is in danger.
Solve this.

527
01:34:18,760 --> 01:34:22,740
Osman Bey...
Son...

528
01:34:22,781 --> 01:34:26,831
You both will grin and bear it.

529
01:34:27,268 --> 01:34:31,608
You will bow down to the decision
of god.

530
01:34:32,279 --> 01:34:39,769
Osman Bey, you will do as the will says.

531
01:36:18,662 --> 01:36:22,992
Osman Bey, will he come?

532
01:36:26,924 --> 01:36:28,964
He will.

533
01:36:33,792 --> 01:36:36,642
-What's your job?
-We are traders.

534
01:36:44,747 --> 01:36:48,417
-Where are your goods?
-In Söğüt.

535
01:36:48,731 --> 01:36:50,481
Söğüt?

536
01:37:02,835 --> 01:37:05,125
Why did you laugh?

537
01:37:10,289 --> 01:37:15,619
If it wasn't for Bamsı Bey, I would have
burned Söğüt.

538
01:38:10,068 --> 01:38:15,678
When we heard that you became the bey,
we ran here. We wanted to congratulate.

539
01:38:15,934 --> 01:38:20,734
Thank you, thank you.

540
01:38:21,187 --> 01:38:23,397
I wanted to talk to you.

541
01:38:23,865 --> 01:38:28,045
I want you to do more than
trading goods.

542
01:38:29,561 --> 01:38:35,431
What can the Kayıs sell to whom?
Other than what we already do.

543
01:38:35,448 --> 01:38:38,389
What can they buy from where?
Tell me.

544
01:38:38,389 --> 01:38:42,979
We accept that as an order, my bey.
From Damascus to Ankara...

545
01:38:43,271 --> 01:38:46,891
...we know all the markets.

546
01:38:47,680 --> 01:38:52,077
We can sell all the goods of the Kayı
in the markets...

547
01:38:52,077 --> 01:38:54,397
...just ask it, Osman Bey.

548
01:38:55,201 --> 01:38:57,381
Thank you.

549
01:38:59,564 --> 01:39:06,604
But the first condition of trade
is that nothing is free, Osman Bey.

550
01:39:22,754 --> 01:39:29,194
What kind of a bey makes his helpers
regret?

551
01:39:32,380 --> 01:39:36,440
Forgive us if he offended you, my bey.

552
01:39:36,865 --> 01:39:39,815
He went over his level.

553
01:39:43,626 --> 01:39:47,816
Every job has different customs and
language.

554
01:39:47,963 --> 01:39:53,829
Do your trade.
And we'll do our job.

555
01:39:53,829 --> 01:39:56,219
Of course.
Of course.

556
01:39:58,964 --> 01:40:03,264
Then, give us a store in Söğüt.

557
01:40:03,468 --> 01:40:07,328
Give us so that we can expand
our trade, my bey.

558
01:40:08,524 --> 01:40:10,184
All right.

559
01:40:11,064 --> 01:40:15,434
Boran Alp, give them a store in Söğüt.

560
01:40:15,612 --> 01:40:18,062
And provide them everything they need.

561
01:40:18,509 --> 01:40:20,519
As you order, my bey.

562
01:40:26,962 --> 01:40:30,502
-May Allah give you luck in your trade.
-Amin.

563
01:40:41,471 --> 01:40:46,061
Such a beadledom could only come
from a trader.

564
01:40:46,661 --> 01:40:51,111
Osman will think that.

565
01:40:58,610 --> 01:41:02,852
-What did he do?
-Give me water, woman.

566
01:41:02,852 --> 01:41:05,792
Give me water, come on.

567
01:41:09,925 --> 01:41:15,095
You put bowstring to my neck, huh?
Do you threaten me with death?

568
01:41:19,189 --> 01:41:21,329
What did he do?

569
01:41:29,685 --> 01:41:33,545
Did he attempt to kill you?

570
01:41:40,682 --> 01:41:43,842
It leads to that.

571
01:41:45,443 --> 01:41:51,343
He hold grudge against me.
He looks for a mistake of mine.

572
01:41:58,755 --> 01:42:00,775
What will we do, then?

573
01:42:02,575 --> 01:42:04,485
What will we do?

574
01:42:05,191 --> 01:42:08,241
Should we leave here?

575
01:42:09,372 --> 01:42:11,782
What should we do?

576
01:42:14,474 --> 01:42:18,334
This is my father's tribe!
My father's tribe!

577
01:42:19,012 --> 01:42:23,092
I was here before them!
I was here!

578
01:42:23,117 --> 01:42:26,147
I will stay and they will leave!

579
01:42:26,233 --> 01:42:29,567
You put a bowstring to my neck, huh?

580
01:42:29,567 --> 01:42:35,497
That Savcı and Gündüz
watched their uncle dying.

581
01:42:35,965 --> 01:42:38,845
Osman...
Osman...

582
01:42:47,227 --> 01:42:50,647
None of them are our friends.

583
01:42:57,232 --> 01:43:02,132
None of them wants us here.

584
01:43:04,164 --> 01:43:07,034
Didn't I tell you, Dündar Bey?

585
01:43:11,586 --> 01:43:16,356
So, what will we do now?

586
01:43:19,238 --> 01:43:22,248
How will we get out of this situation?

587
01:44:20,376 --> 01:44:22,316
I will ask for forgiveness.

588
01:44:25,762 --> 01:44:30,782
I will ask for forgiveness from my nephew.

589
01:44:41,212 --> 01:44:42,652
Dündar Bey.

590
01:44:43,532 --> 01:44:47,572
You were like a hungry wolf
a moment ago.

591
01:44:47,978 --> 01:44:54,468
What's wrong? Happened that you
turned into a sheep?

592
01:44:56,225 --> 01:44:57,805
Woman.

593
01:44:59,965 --> 01:45:02,065
From now.

594
01:45:03,275 --> 01:45:07,925
I'll be a wolf under a sheep's disguise.

595
01:45:09,317 --> 01:45:15,227
A sheep in the tribe, a wolf outside.

596
01:45:17,856 --> 01:45:22,226
Firstly, I'll gain Osman's trust.

597
01:45:23,529 --> 01:45:29,499
Then, I'll whip that bowstring...

598
01:45:30,579 --> 01:45:33,070
...around his neck.

599
01:45:33,738 --> 01:45:36,458
Around his neck.

600
01:45:43,228 --> 01:45:45,948
You'll be on good terms with Bala.

601
01:45:46,700 --> 01:45:49,280
You won't argue with Selcan.

602
01:45:50,202 --> 01:45:55,512
For a while, play this game. Make them
think that they have us.

603
01:45:56,144 --> 01:45:59,844
They should tend to their business
and forget about us.

604
01:46:00,478 --> 01:46:02,978
When they expect the least.

605
01:46:05,291 --> 01:46:09,311
We'll come back again.
Again.

606
01:46:40,318 --> 01:46:47,008
We invited and
you honored us.

607
01:46:48,107 --> 01:46:50,600
Thank you all.

608
01:46:50,600 --> 01:46:55,760
May Allah never takes you from us.

609
01:46:55,768 --> 01:46:58,018
-Amin.
-Amin.

610
01:46:58,858 --> 01:47:02,138
Of course, we'll come, my nephew.

611
01:47:02,621 --> 01:47:07,431
From now, you are our bey.

612
01:47:13,004 --> 01:47:20,104
Even though I'm older, I should
act accordingly to your word.

613
01:47:22,051 --> 01:47:27,321
I made a mistake.

614
01:47:31,229 --> 01:47:38,209
From now, it's your place to forgive.

615
01:47:49,976 --> 01:47:54,546
Will you forgive me?

616
01:48:43,907 --> 01:48:48,207
That's why I wanted this dinner.

617
01:48:52,152 --> 01:48:58,662
To end the fights and rivalries
end between us.

618
01:49:04,839 --> 01:49:09,929
Everyone should know their place
and their age.

619
01:49:14,282 --> 01:49:17,822
From now, everyone should treat
each other accordingly.

620
01:49:24,645 --> 01:49:29,595
Uncle, if you ask for forgiveness.

621
01:49:32,689 --> 01:49:36,069
If you say that it won't happen again.

622
01:49:41,567 --> 01:49:44,707
Then, I'll forgive you, uncle.

623
01:50:12,460 --> 01:50:17,260
From now, we should come together
in such nights.

624
01:50:18,466 --> 01:50:21,136
Share our breads.

625
01:50:21,725 --> 01:50:27,671
We should share so that we can
remember that...

626
01:50:27,671 --> 01:50:32,231
...we are relatives,
that we carry the same blood.

627
01:50:37,787 --> 01:50:44,930
Tell me, mother. Is it appropriate for
us to be estranged from each other?

628
01:50:45,320 --> 01:50:47,640
Of course not.

629
01:50:49,422 --> 01:50:52,012
Of course not, son.

630
01:50:55,772 --> 01:51:00,892
Every encounter is an opportunity
for penitence.

631
01:51:04,665 --> 01:51:07,795
Every unification...

632
01:51:07,938 --> 01:51:11,628
...is the door of starting again.

633
01:51:12,535 --> 01:51:14,685
You spoke well, aunt.

634
01:51:16,307 --> 01:51:21,007
Many times, when I was performing
ablution, I thought the same.

635
01:51:21,531 --> 01:51:27,461
I tell myself, you freshened your intentions,
don't break yours before the other does.

636
01:51:31,138 --> 01:51:33,718
You are right, brother.

637
01:51:34,803 --> 01:51:40,933
I wish we can hold ours, even if the others
breaks theirs.

638
01:51:45,385 --> 01:51:47,205
Gündüz Bey.

639
01:51:47,897 --> 01:51:51,337
This is a word worthy of sufistics.

640
01:51:52,296 --> 01:51:57,306
My nephew has the heart of a fakir.

641
01:51:58,376 --> 01:52:03,044
Even if one wants to fight,
it can't be against him.

642
01:52:03,044 --> 01:52:10,304
His heart is so pure that, whatever
he says is true.

643
01:52:10,919 --> 01:52:13,119
Thank you, uncle.

644
01:52:18,629 --> 01:52:22,289
We, women, should take our
lessons from these words.

645
01:52:24,045 --> 01:52:28,810
It's life, we might break each other...

646
01:52:28,810 --> 01:52:33,770
...but we should have the dignity
left to look at each other in the face.

647
01:52:42,816 --> 01:52:47,886
Of course...
Of course, Bala Hatun.

648
01:52:50,746 --> 01:52:54,716
Back in the time, we would get along
so well.

649
01:52:59,879 --> 01:53:02,769
Let us be like that again.

650
01:53:06,696 --> 01:53:08,796
Inshallah.

651
01:53:09,154 --> 01:53:11,474
Inshallah.

652
01:53:12,078 --> 01:53:15,608
Inshallah.
Inshallah.

653
01:53:19,828 --> 01:53:24,128
The tongue has no bones.

654
01:53:24,735 --> 01:53:30,050
And bad memories can't get forgotten
easily.

655
01:53:30,050 --> 01:53:36,110
But, we shouldn't get to the point that
we can't look each other in the face.

656
01:53:39,271 --> 01:53:44,461
Mashallah to our pretty khatun.
Mashallah.

657
01:53:58,178 --> 01:54:01,558
This peace should take as long
as it can.

658
01:54:02,882 --> 01:54:08,492
In my part, I won't be the one
who breaks it.

659
01:54:22,008 --> 01:54:26,808
If someone takes a step for me,
I'll take two for them.

660
01:54:27,346 --> 01:54:30,006
No one should doubt it.

661
01:54:33,111 --> 01:54:35,641
As long as it's sincere.

662
01:54:38,616 --> 01:54:40,656
Thank you.

663
01:54:41,907 --> 01:54:47,837
So, my nephew Bayhoca.
Say a few words.

664
01:54:49,207 --> 01:54:54,860
How is the situation in Konya?
How are the madrasahs? Tell us.

665
01:54:58,580 --> 01:55:01,870
Nothing can grow in the soil
that Mongols step on, uncle.

666
01:55:03,298 --> 01:55:06,638
Science gets its share from that.

667
01:55:07,888 --> 01:55:10,868
Do you say that scholars are dispersing?

668
01:55:11,575 --> 01:55:18,335
Yes, uncle. But not to east,
they are going to west.

669
01:55:21,542 --> 01:55:26,042
-Are they going to the borders?
-To the borders.

670
01:55:31,542 --> 01:55:38,512
Brother. What should we do to
convince those scholars.

671
01:55:40,149 --> 01:55:44,339
Scholars need madrasahs, Osman Bey.

672
01:55:45,654 --> 01:55:48,452
Madrasahs need a city.

673
01:55:48,452 --> 01:55:52,669
A city needs a state.

674
01:55:52,669 --> 01:55:58,099
It needs a state.
It needs a state.

675
01:56:04,589 --> 01:56:06,629
It needs a state.

676
01:56:29,224 --> 01:56:31,124
Come on.

677
01:56:32,954 --> 01:56:36,284
With the name of Allah.

678
01:56:37,144 --> 01:56:40,364
Go on.
Enjoy your meal.

679
01:57:32,927 --> 01:57:35,797
I informed the frontiersmen.

680
01:57:36,019 --> 01:57:40,379
-Tomorrow, they'll come to Söğüt.
-May it be good, Osman Bey.

681
01:57:40,882 --> 01:57:43,732
Do you wish to celebrate your title?

682
01:57:45,798 --> 01:57:48,408
We already finished that, uncle.

683
01:57:54,240 --> 01:58:00,570
From now, I want to conquer
İnegöl Castle.

684
01:58:59,826 --> 01:59:03,516
With the name of Allah.

685
01:59:31,695 --> 01:59:33,935
Cerkutay is coming.

686
01:59:39,864 --> 01:59:43,534
Come, Cerkutay.
Come.

687
01:59:51,648 --> 01:59:55,868
'May I come?', you should say, Cerkutay.

688
01:59:56,747 --> 01:59:59,357
May I come?

689
02:00:59,426 --> 02:01:00,746
Cerkutay.

690
02:01:03,398 --> 02:01:04,848
Come here.

691
02:01:08,655 --> 02:01:09,915
Come here.

692
02:01:21,081 --> 02:01:22,851
Cerkutay.

693
02:01:23,289 --> 02:01:26,189
Don't you have a mother, father...

694
02:01:26,923 --> 02:01:29,053
or any brothers?

695
02:01:32,765 --> 02:01:34,125
They're dead.

696
02:01:38,119 --> 02:01:42,119
Did you spend all your life in wars?

697
02:01:42,610 --> 02:01:44,380
Don't you have a lover?

698
02:01:48,441 --> 02:01:51,941
A warrior's lover is his gun, right?

699
02:01:56,731 --> 02:01:58,451
Cerkutay...

700
02:01:58,799 --> 02:02:00,589
Yes.

701
02:02:00,910 --> 02:02:04,140
A warrior's lover is his gun.

702
02:02:06,558 --> 02:02:07,628
However...

703
02:02:07,754 --> 02:02:08,984
Cerkutay...

704
02:02:09,901 --> 02:02:12,261
love is necessary.

705
02:02:13,562 --> 02:02:15,582
Someone other than you.

706
02:02:16,350 --> 02:02:21,810
Loving someone more than yourself is hard.

707
02:02:27,719 --> 02:02:29,489
I'd love to...

708
02:02:31,413 --> 02:02:33,123
love someone else...

709
02:02:34,270 --> 02:02:37,300
more than myself...

710
02:02:38,726 --> 02:02:40,186
I'd love that.

711
02:02:41,672 --> 02:02:44,662
You're young, Cerkutay.
You're young.

712
02:02:44,667 --> 02:02:46,847
You will love.
You will be loved.

713
02:02:47,095 --> 02:02:52,475
You'll understand how good it is.

714
02:03:13,989 --> 02:03:16,579
My Bey, you shouldn't fight anymore.

715
02:03:22,508 --> 02:03:24,418
Why?

716
02:03:25,340 --> 02:03:27,750
My whole family is dead.

717
02:03:28,493 --> 02:03:30,543
I don't want you to die.

718
02:03:40,010 --> 02:03:41,460
Cerkutay...

719
02:03:42,964 --> 02:03:46,284
You've just burned my heart.

720
02:03:55,071 --> 02:04:00,101
Cerkutay, I have more years.

721
02:04:01,953 --> 02:04:05,273
I'll raise you.

722
02:04:06,492 --> 02:04:08,472
Listen to me well.

723
02:04:08,619 --> 02:04:12,619
I was my Ertuğrul Bey's Bamsı.

724
02:04:15,615 --> 02:04:17,495
Now, you...

725
02:04:17,995 --> 02:04:21,095
will be Osman Bey's Bamsı.

726
02:04:22,027 --> 02:04:25,217
You'll be Osman Bey's Bamsı.

727
02:04:35,346 --> 02:04:38,226
Will I have a beard like yours?

728
02:04:44,219 --> 02:04:46,349
Oh, Cerkutay.

729
02:04:47,870 --> 02:04:51,870
You made me smile, may Allah
make you smile too.

730
02:05:09,033 --> 02:05:10,783
I'm ready, my Bey.

731
02:05:14,048 --> 02:05:16,378
Tell me everything.

732
02:05:39,217 --> 02:05:43,217
Will you ask for support from Beys
to conquer İnegöl, Osman Bey?

733
02:05:45,736 --> 02:05:47,916
Yes, brother.

734
02:05:48,755 --> 02:05:49,955
But...

735
02:05:52,811 --> 02:05:55,501
İnegöl Castle is hard to conquer.

736
02:05:56,441 --> 02:05:58,131
It's tough.

737
02:06:03,457 --> 02:06:04,767
Firstly...

738
02:06:06,830 --> 02:06:09,220
I want to see the preparations.

739
02:06:10,376 --> 02:06:12,076
Thank you.

740
02:06:12,705 --> 02:06:14,935
You do everything right.

741
02:06:19,844 --> 02:06:21,424
What if they don't support?

742
02:06:21,519 --> 02:06:24,869
The Beys are valiants who
fought next to my father.

743
02:06:28,132 --> 02:06:30,122
We'll convince them.

744
02:06:31,113 --> 02:06:35,993
- What if they don't support us anyway?
- We'll tell them...

745
02:06:36,162 --> 02:06:38,822
the importance of the situation
and the idea of war.

746
02:06:39,993 --> 02:06:44,553
We have to be together
for freedom and justice.

747
02:06:49,617 --> 02:06:51,247
If needed...

748
02:06:51,748 --> 02:06:54,748
we'll go to...

749
02:06:57,198 --> 02:06:58,808
Germiyanids ourselves.

750
02:07:03,837 --> 02:07:06,577
It's my father's will...

751
02:07:06,606 --> 02:07:07,996
and...

752
02:07:10,898 --> 02:07:12,908
my will.

753
02:07:20,402 --> 02:07:21,842
Brother...

754
02:07:23,547 --> 02:07:25,387
I want something from you.

755
02:07:25,551 --> 02:07:27,061
Yes, brother.

756
02:07:29,318 --> 02:07:34,088
I want you to meet Nikola in a safe place.

757
02:07:37,687 --> 02:07:40,037
Tell him that I want peace.

758
02:07:46,742 --> 02:07:49,942
- Will he believe me?
- He'll want to believe you, uncle.

759
02:07:52,406 --> 02:07:55,616
We killed his soldiers last time.

760
02:07:56,050 --> 02:07:59,120
He won't be able to fight without a
support.

761
02:08:00,739 --> 02:08:03,879
Why do we want peace?

762
02:08:06,686 --> 02:08:09,796
I want to stop him until I reach my goal.

763
02:08:12,051 --> 02:08:14,491
He'll think he's wasting our time.

764
02:08:15,387 --> 02:08:16,917
However...

765
02:08:18,233 --> 02:08:20,803
we'll be digging his grave.

766
02:08:28,984 --> 02:08:32,104
Don't worry.
I'll meet him.

767
02:08:36,445 --> 02:08:39,165
Are there any duties for me?

768
02:08:50,733 --> 02:08:54,213
Osman Bey's duties are dangerous, Bayhoca.

769
02:08:55,783 --> 02:08:57,103
Firstly...

770
02:08:58,544 --> 02:09:01,064
ask for permission from your
mother and father.

771
02:09:07,359 --> 02:09:10,199
Ask me later.

772
02:10:26,409 --> 02:10:29,179
Is it all done?

773
02:10:29,732 --> 02:10:32,792
Yes, my Bey.
These goods are the last ones.

774
02:10:36,261 --> 02:10:39,881
This place will be opened tomorrow.

775
02:10:40,182 --> 02:10:43,212
We promised to Osman Bey.

776
02:10:45,492 --> 02:10:47,602
Thank you, valiants.

777
02:10:58,274 --> 02:11:00,544
Salam Alaikum.

778
02:11:03,685 --> 02:11:05,565
Alaikum Salam.

779
02:11:13,246 --> 02:11:15,996
Is the news you'll tell me...

780
02:11:16,042 --> 02:11:18,862
about the feast in Söğüt?

781
02:11:19,811 --> 02:11:21,871
So you know.

782
02:11:22,800 --> 02:11:24,800
I have ears.

783
02:11:25,490 --> 02:11:27,270
I can hear too.

784
02:11:30,767 --> 02:11:32,367
Then...

785
02:11:33,281 --> 02:11:36,391
you may know Osman is taking action.

786
02:11:37,218 --> 02:11:41,218
I've heard that he'll gather all the Beys
in Söğüt.

787
02:11:41,769 --> 02:11:44,369
Then, you know.

788
02:11:44,520 --> 02:11:48,100
- You know why.
- It's obvious why.

789
02:11:49,184 --> 02:11:51,784
He'll gather all of the Uç Beys.

790
02:11:51,851 --> 02:11:55,851
He'll attack İnegöl with a big army.

791
02:11:58,146 --> 02:12:00,676
It's Osman.
He'll do it.

792
02:12:01,509 --> 02:12:04,289
Stop acting as if you're not afraid.

793
02:12:04,749 --> 02:12:08,749
If he succeeds, he won't just
conquer İnegöl...

794
02:12:09,102 --> 02:12:13,102
you know what comes next...

795
02:12:13,696 --> 02:12:17,846
- after İnegöl.
- What are you thinking?

796
02:12:24,740 --> 02:12:28,740
Beys won't come to Söğüt tomorrow...

797
02:12:31,301 --> 02:12:33,811
their corpses will.

798
02:12:35,800 --> 02:12:37,680
All of them?

799
02:12:39,010 --> 02:12:40,710
Yes.

800
02:12:53,436 --> 02:12:56,586
We should frighten Osman.

801
02:12:59,283 --> 02:13:01,673
We shouldn't let him sleep comfortably.

802
02:13:04,432 --> 02:13:09,322
He should see
the corpses in his nightmares.

803
02:13:45,014 --> 02:13:46,304
Look, son.

804
02:13:47,756 --> 02:13:49,926
Next to there belongs to Kayıs.

805
02:13:51,275 --> 02:13:56,295
- Our Ertuğrul Bey's lands.
- We should go to Ertuğrul Bey's grave.

806
02:13:58,308 --> 02:14:01,228
Yes, we should.

807
02:14:01,305 --> 02:14:04,775
- Have you ever seen Osman Bey, father?
- Yes.

808
02:14:05,834 --> 02:14:08,594
He was young at that time.

809
02:14:09,317 --> 02:14:12,547
Ertuğrul Bey took him with himself
when he was coming to our tent.

810
02:14:13,341 --> 02:14:16,551
It was obvious that he'd be a good Bey.

811
02:14:16,582 --> 02:14:19,332
Why does he want us in Söğüt?

812
02:14:20,339 --> 02:14:24,769
Osman Bey wants to do what his father did.

813
02:14:25,539 --> 02:14:28,529
That's why he has invited us.

814
02:15:01,057 --> 02:15:03,597
That' what we'll do.

815
02:15:09,055 --> 02:15:10,575
Now.

816
02:15:16,555 --> 02:15:17,875
Father!

817
02:15:20,591 --> 02:15:21,461
Father!

818
02:15:29,667 --> 02:15:31,277
Father!

819
02:15:31,814 --> 02:15:35,814
Father!;
Father!

820
02:15:41,599 --> 02:15:47,049
Father! Father!
Father!

821
02:15:52,250 --> 02:15:53,980
Okay.
Enough.

822
02:15:54,966 --> 02:15:56,986
Enough.

823
02:15:57,315 --> 02:15:59,275
Father!

824
02:16:03,318 --> 02:16:06,188
The child will bring his father's corpse
to Söğüt.

825
02:16:07,893 --> 02:16:10,683
Osman Bey will see that we are peaceful.

826
02:16:33,751 --> 02:16:35,961
Osman Bey is coming!

827
02:17:23,621 --> 02:17:25,811
Long live Osman Bey!

828
02:17:36,920 --> 02:17:38,850
Thank you!

829
02:17:42,255 --> 02:17:43,935
May it be easy.

830
02:17:44,550 --> 02:17:45,630
May it be fruitful.

831
02:17:45,686 --> 02:17:47,936
- Welcome, my Bey.
- Thank you.

832
02:17:48,807 --> 02:17:51,867
Welcome, Osman Bey.

833
02:17:52,885 --> 02:17:56,885
- Thank you.
- I congratulate you for being the new Bey.

834
02:17:57,803 --> 02:17:59,833
Thank you.

835
02:18:00,080 --> 02:18:01,680
Mashallah to you.

836
02:18:08,307 --> 02:18:10,937
- Take it.
- Thank you, Osman Bey.

837
02:18:11,326 --> 02:18:14,266
- Thank you, Osman Bey.
- Thank you. Enjoy it.

838
02:18:14,660 --> 02:18:16,530
Come on.

839
02:18:23,846 --> 02:18:29,176
Welcome, my Bey. May Allah
give you a long life.

840
02:18:29,330 --> 02:18:33,150
- Amin.
- You came with your goodness.

841
02:18:33,211 --> 02:18:36,441
- Amin.
- May your Beyhood will be good.

842
02:18:39,964 --> 02:18:41,974
Thank you.

843
02:18:51,660 --> 02:18:54,430
- Welcome, my Bey.
- Welcome, Osman Bey.

844
02:18:54,852 --> 02:18:56,752
Thank you.

845
02:18:57,172 --> 02:18:58,522
Thank you.

846
02:19:00,140 --> 02:19:02,350
Mashallah.

847
02:19:06,331 --> 02:19:09,531
- It suits you.
- Thank you.

848
02:19:15,468 --> 02:19:18,428
Thank you. May Allah give you a long life.

849
02:19:32,416 --> 02:19:35,526
Welcome, Osman Bey.
Welcome.

850
02:19:37,575 --> 02:19:41,575
Our Beylic will grow. Inshaallah...

851
02:19:41,878 --> 02:19:44,048
our trade will grow.

852
02:19:44,905 --> 02:19:46,775
We'll establish new bazaars.

853
02:19:47,225 --> 02:19:51,965
We'll take our goods to
places we can't reach now.

854
02:19:54,065 --> 02:19:57,775
You're right, My Bey but
it requires a big preparation.

855
02:19:57,808 --> 02:20:01,228
The craftsmen and the merchants should
be prepared.

856
02:20:02,503 --> 02:20:04,303
Yes.

857
02:20:04,616 --> 02:20:06,876
You're right.
What do you sell?

858
02:20:07,137 --> 02:20:10,907
I sell honey, butter and tallow.

859
02:20:12,300 --> 02:20:13,890
Here.

860
02:20:15,795 --> 02:20:17,955
Mashallah.

861
02:20:19,588 --> 02:20:21,698
- Thank you.
- May it be Halal.

862
02:20:21,787 --> 02:20:25,787
- May it be Halal.
- My brother is doing cereal trade.

863
02:20:31,813 --> 02:20:32,943
How much goods...

864
02:20:34,260 --> 02:20:37,690
- do you bring?
- I bring goods full of four cars.

865
02:20:37,758 --> 02:20:40,468
And with two horses full of goods.

866
02:20:41,594 --> 02:20:42,954
What if...

867
02:20:45,012 --> 02:20:47,372
you bring goods to Bursa?

868
02:20:52,360 --> 02:20:56,360
To İznik? Konya?

869
02:20:57,403 --> 02:20:58,803
Sivas?

870
02:20:58,935 --> 02:21:02,435
I'll need countless cars and horses.

871
02:21:02,691 --> 02:21:05,641
We'll need more men.

872
02:21:06,354 --> 02:21:09,104
And production should be boosted.

873
02:21:10,718 --> 02:21:12,378
To boost the production and...

874
02:21:13,153 --> 02:21:16,203
to send the goods to everywhere...

875
02:21:16,731 --> 02:21:18,921
I'll do everything I can.

876
02:21:19,506 --> 02:21:23,596
We'll make inconvenient
people stronger together.

877
02:21:24,717 --> 02:21:28,717
So that our people will fight.

878
02:21:29,992 --> 02:21:31,892
They will be strong.

879
02:21:33,415 --> 02:21:35,355
What I should do is...

880
02:21:36,553 --> 02:21:39,223
to make the people stronger.

881
02:21:40,531 --> 02:21:45,571
I'll meet with merchants in a short time
and discuss the problem.

882
02:21:45,600 --> 02:21:48,470
Thank you, my Bey.

883
02:22:00,527 --> 02:22:02,457
Osman Bey.

884
02:22:03,136 --> 02:22:06,256
- Salam Alaikum.
- Alaikum Salam.

885
02:22:07,670 --> 02:22:11,800
I congratulate your Beyhood, Osman Bey.
I tried to come as soon as possible.

886
02:22:12,861 --> 02:22:16,221
Thank you.

887
02:22:18,741 --> 02:22:21,011
Are you ready?

888
02:22:21,461 --> 02:22:23,941
The whole Kastamonu is waiting.

889
02:22:24,047 --> 02:22:27,247
We're waiting for Geyhatu to come
back from Tabriz.

890
02:22:27,908 --> 02:22:31,678
We are ready for anything with the
help of Allah.

891
02:22:31,817 --> 02:22:34,797
We have one thing
to do before Geyhatu comes back.

892
02:22:35,570 --> 02:22:38,680
I'll have all the power of Uç Beys and...

893
02:22:38,852 --> 02:22:41,092
conquer İnegöl.

894
02:22:41,501 --> 02:22:44,081
We should be sure of them...

895
02:22:44,877 --> 02:22:47,287
so that we can be powerful when
Geyhatu comes back.

896
02:22:47,287 --> 02:22:52,159
You should have your Alps and Uç Beys.

897
02:22:52,269 --> 02:22:55,673
Then we'll do what we should do.

898
02:22:56,197 --> 02:22:57,527
Thank you.

899
02:23:01,370 --> 02:23:05,120
So, you did it.
Congratulations.

900
02:23:05,360 --> 02:23:08,520
Thanks to you, Osman Bey.

901
02:23:08,720 --> 02:23:10,750
Thank you.

902
02:23:10,956 --> 02:23:17,066
We'll make so many good things together
with the blessing of your Beyhood.

903
02:23:17,767 --> 02:23:18,567
You...

904
02:23:20,097 --> 02:23:23,157
take care of what I said.

905
02:23:23,541 --> 02:23:26,661
I'm waiting for
your information about new bazaars.

906
02:23:27,561 --> 02:23:29,771
Don't worry, my Bey.

907
02:23:31,859 --> 02:23:33,579
May it be easy.

908
02:23:44,801 --> 02:23:47,501
Why aren't the Beys here?

909
02:23:49,090 --> 02:23:51,230
They killed my father!

910
02:23:59,705 --> 02:24:02,445
- Father!
- It's Hasan Bey's son.

911
02:24:04,323 --> 02:24:06,803
Hasan Bey?

912
02:24:11,893 --> 02:24:14,163
They killed my father!

913
02:24:14,578 --> 02:24:16,878
They killed my father!

914
02:24:23,833 --> 02:24:28,563
Take my father's revenge, Osman Bey.
He was going to fight for you.

915
02:24:50,636 --> 02:24:52,996
Wait, Osman.

916
02:24:54,314 --> 02:24:57,024
It's just a beginning.

917
02:25:00,413 --> 02:25:01,703
Don't...

918
02:25:02,950 --> 02:25:04,900
worry.

919
02:25:29,243 --> 02:25:30,563
Father!

920
02:26:22,620 --> 02:26:23,890
My Bey.

921
02:26:24,132 --> 02:26:27,132
They killed three Beys.

922
02:26:27,721 --> 02:26:29,901
Fazlı Bey, İlyas Bey and Turan Bey.

923
02:27:04,026 --> 02:27:05,976
So, they knew it.

924
02:27:06,364 --> 02:27:09,264
They knew who would come.

925
02:27:36,693 --> 02:27:39,853
What's written on that paper, Gündüz Bey?

926
02:27:40,878 --> 02:27:43,178
It's just a beginning.

927
02:27:43,269 --> 02:27:46,399
Until all of the Turks die.

928
02:28:08,708 --> 02:28:10,458
From now on...

929
02:28:12,423 --> 02:28:14,553
I'll breathe death...

930
02:28:15,004 --> 02:28:17,344
and cause distress!

931
02:28:27,725 --> 02:28:30,215
If anyone is...

932
02:28:31,115 --> 02:28:33,755
included in this...

933
02:28:36,945 --> 02:28:39,335
I'll...

934
02:28:40,592 --> 02:28:44,592
rip their lungs off...

935
02:28:45,258 --> 02:28:47,778
and make the dogs eat them!

936
02:28:51,445 --> 02:28:54,285
If I don't take their revenge...

937
02:28:55,463 --> 02:28:56,733
then...

938
02:28:57,984 --> 02:29:00,714
I'm not the son of Ertuğrul Ghazi...

939
02:29:01,343 --> 02:29:05,343
Osman Bey.

940
02:29:17,533 --> 02:29:35,163
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com